{"user": "how do I knwo which move is the best", "user_ts": "2026-08-21T12:35:11.841158+00:00", "assistant": "To find the best endgame move, don\u2019t ask \u201cwhich flips most now?\u201d Ask:\n\n1. **Does it give White a corner next?**  \n   Corners like **h1** or **a8** can\u2019t be flipped back.\n\n2. **What moves will White have after my move?**  \n   A good move often leaves White with very few legal replies, or forces a bad one.\n\n3. **Count the final result, not the immediate flips.**  \n   Mentally play: Black move \u2192 White reply \u2192 Black move, and see who gets the last big flips/corners.\n\nFor this board, compare your legal moves by asking:  \n- If I play near **h1** or **a8**, can White take that corner next?  \n- Does my move reduce White\u2019s choices or open new good ones?", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-21T12:35:21.460206+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-21T12:35:24.139494+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Solution Request"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 3}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 1.0}, "per_model": {"sonnet": ["Solution Request"], "gpt": ["Solution Request"], "llama": ["Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "consensus": ["General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Hint": 2, "Prompt": 3}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Hint": 0.6666666666666666, "Prompt": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "llama": ["General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "sonnet": ["General Principle", "Prompt"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint", "Prompt"]}}
{"user": "how do I know which coins will flip?", "user_ts": "2026-08-21T12:36:25.348859+00:00", "assistant": "A disc flips when it is in a **straight line** between your new Black disc and another Black disc, with **only White discs in between**.\n\nCheck all 8 directions: horizontal, vertical, diagonal.\n\nOn this board, if Black plays:\n\n- **g2** flips **f2** and **g3**\n- **b6** flips **c6, d6, c5, c7**\n- **a7** flips **a6 and b7\u2013g7**\n- **b8** flips **c7 and d6**\n\nBut remember: in the endgame, **flipping the most now isn\u2019t always best**\u2014also check whether it gives White a corner or good reply.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-21T12:36:37.142142+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-21T12:36:38.958509+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Move Verdict": 1, "Local Justification": 1, "Hint": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Move Verdict": 0.3333333333333333, "Local Justification": 0.3333333333333333, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Move Verdict", "Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "General Principle", "Hint"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
{"user": "how much of this game is skill vs luck", "user_ts": "2026-08-21T12:36:58.332478+00:00", "assistant": "Othello is **almost entirely skill**: no dice, no hidden cards, no random events. The only \u201cluck\u201d is if an opponent happens to miss something.\n\nIn this position, use skill by checking:\n- **Corners**: a corner like **a8** can never be flipped.\n- **Squares next to corners**: like **b8**, can be risky if they give access to a corner.\n- **Mobility**: after your move, how many replies does White get? Fewer is usually better.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-21T12:37:04.096402+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-21T12:37:06.096028+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Board Report": 1, "Local Justification": 1, "Hint": 1, "Prompt": 1}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Board Report": 0.3333333333333333, "Local Justification": 0.3333333333333333, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333, "Prompt": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle"], "llama": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
